# `x default y` (decision nullish-split): y when x raises or is ø, a falsy x kept (`0 default 10` is 0,
# `parse_json("{oops") default []` is []); `x ?? y` replaces only ø, `x or y` every falsy x. Its other spellings note
# warp's word. Early sugar, so core/passes/tries.warp reads the try. A match arm `default: v` is a key, no phrase:
# still the catch-all
rewrite $a otherwise $b => $a default $b where alias
rewrite $a failing $b => $a default $b where alias
rewrite $a except $b => $a default $b where alias
rewrite $a rescue $b => $a default $b where alias
# (a class on the right is no fallback: `matrix default Dense` names the protocol's default class, extensions/protocols.warp)
rewrite $a default $b => try $a except $b where not $b is type
